  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: AppComm 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "Your local cancer center posts updates about a newly approved treatment
    and asks for feedback on how treatment and safety information are shared with
    the community.\n\n<b>Once a new treatment is approved, health systems rely on
    official follow-up reports\u2014not community feedback\u2014to improve how safety
    information is shared.</b>\n\nIs this <b>true</b> or <b>false</b>?"
  explanation: Community feedback remains important even after a new treatment is
    approved. Advocates and patients help identify what information is unclear, missing,
    or most important to the community. Their input helps health systems share safety
    updates in ways that are more understandable, trusted, and useful.
  correctAnswer: False
  incorrectAnswer1: True
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Community Advocate
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Approval
